entry.summary:
When building scalable systems, one of the biggest challenges developers face is performance bottlenecks.

A bottleneck happens when part of the system slows down the overall performance.  
Below are the most common areas where bottlenecks appear and how to handle them.
Indexing: Is a database optimization technique that improves the speed of data retrieval operations on a table.


Optimize queries: Write efficient SQL queries and use indexes where appropriate.  


Batch operations: Instead of executing multiple single-row inserts using create in Laravel, use bulk inserts with insert.



Example in Laravel:
  // Slow: multiple INSERT queries (one per row)
  foreach ($data as $row) {
      User::create($row);
  }

  // Fast: one bulk INSERT query
  User::insert($data);

